    "thesis": "Boris Berezovsky epitomized post-Soviet Russia's transition, transforming the chaotic collapse of the state into a kleptocracy by deeply intertwining organized crime, business, and government through corrupt privatization schemes and political manipulation. His rise demonstrates how a lack of a healthy state and society led to the systematic looting of national wealth and the discrediting of nascent democracy and free markets."
